<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3321 shares a unique co-orbital configuration with the Moon about Earth, but is unaffected by the Moon's gravity.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>It has a much weaker gravitational field than leading theories of relativity suggest is possible</p>
</blockquote>
<p>how can it be unaffected by the moon's gravity yet itself have a gravitational field</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3321 is very stable, has no electromagnetic field, and emits only trace amounts of particle radiation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>how can you take a picture of it if it does not interact electromagnetically? how can you take a thermal image of it if it only emits trace amount of particle radiation (and therefore no heat)?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It is possible to enter SCP-3321 from any direction in 3-dimensional space, and can be done so without causing damage to spacecraft.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>since its entrance is only 3 dimensional, which of the three dimensions does it have? x,y,z, and t are our options; so if it lacks t, then nothing would be able to enter it for starters&#8230;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>its exit exists in 2-dimensional space.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>how could they possibly know this?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Once entered, SCP-3321 leads to SCP-3321-1, an area that is believed to be an uncharted location in deep space.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>is this the 2 dimensional part? how can 4 dimensional objects exist and function in a 2 dimensional space? it lacks a direction and time&#8230;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A tethered camera was then extended into the surface of SCP-3321.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>that is a pretty damn long tether for that camera</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;It looks like a cloud, but… heavier, if that makes sense. Almost tangible.&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>clouds are tangible and also very heavy. the average weight of a cumulous cloud is ~1 million pounds.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Nearly five years after the previous voyage, a solo expedition was conducted into SCP-3321-1.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>i find this absolutely ridiculous. there is no way any agency would allow a solo mission into something like a wormhole that is not at all understood. by this time, 5 years have passed but nothing is mentioned about the testing done on the foam samples that have been brought back.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Well… what if it actually is? What if SCP-3321-1 is the edge of the universe? What if all those theories about the universe being boundless are wrong, and I'm traveling towards the barrier between everything and nothing?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>stahp</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It looks kind of like… it looks like… oh my God.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>[THE REMAINDER OF THIS AUDIO TRANSMISSION HAS BEEN REDACTED]</p>
</blockquote>
<p>other than to hide what she sees from us, the reader, why would the foundation redact this part of the message in a *file made specifically to detail what it was*?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The full transcript is as follows:</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Someone else is out here—no, everyone is. It's so loud, and they're all crying. I shouldn't have come. ███ ███ ██ █████ ███ █████ ████ ██ ████ ███ ████ ████████ ███ ████ █████████ █████████ ██ ███ ██████ ███ ██████ ███ ████ ███████████ ████. He wanted to show us, but why did you have to send me?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>hmm full transcript, and all the important bits are blacked out. really makes you think.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;We have decided it is in the best interest of the Foundation that, frankly, nobody knows about that.&quot; —O5-11</p>
</blockquote>
<p>on what grounds? really gets the brain strained.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<em>For the sake of our mobile readers, please collapse long posts. ~Zyn</em>
<p>all that aside, interesting read. i like scifi and i like seeing what interesting ideas people come up with for things having to do with space travel. i'm gonna give you an upvote. :)</p>

